## Stack

- **Language**: ArkTS (TypeScript-derived; HarmonyOS-specific decorators)
- **Framework**: ArkUI (declarative, similar to Compose / SwiftUI)
- **IDE**: DevEco Studio {{deveco_version}}
- **Build tool**: hvigorw (Gradle-equivalent for HarmonyOS)
- **State management**: `@State` / `@Prop` / `@Link` decorators + AppStorage
- **Minimum API**: HarmonyOS NEXT API {{min_api}} (e.g. 11)
- **Test runner**: hypium (built into DevEco)

## Build / install / runtime verify

The canonical recipe is in `<docs-hub>/00_shared-rules/verify-build.md`. Quick reference:

```bash
# Build a debug HAP (HarmonyOS Ability Package)
./hvigorw assembleHap --mode debug
# Windows: hvigorw.bat assembleHap --mode debug
# verify: https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-hvigor-build-overview

# Install on connected device (USB / wifi pair)
hdc install -r build/default/outputs/default/{{hap_file}}.hap
# verify: https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/harmonyos-guides/hdc

# Launch a specific Ability
hdc shell aa start -a {{ability_name}} -b {{bundle_name}}

# Runtime log (filter by bundle for noise control)
hdc shell hilog | grep {{bundle_name}} | tee .ai-workspace/diag/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)-${TASK}-log.txt

# Screenshot
hdc shell snapshot_display -f /data/local/tmp/screen.png
hdc file recv /data/local/tmp/screen.png .ai-workspace/screenshots/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)-${TASK}-after.png

# Lint
./hvigorw lint
```

> **Cross-OS note**: DevEco Studio runs on macOS / Windows / Linux. `hvigorw` works in PowerShell, Git Bash, or bash. `hdc` is Huawei's `adb` equivalent — same flow.

